      "side": 1,
      "message": "http://aosp/1341673 synced android-mainline to the latest inline encryption patches, including https://lkml.kernel.org/linux-f2fs-devel/20200617075732.213198-4-satyat@google.com for f2fs.  The other ACK branches are still on an older version of the inline encryption patches.  Among many other things, that means this \u0027f2fs_set_bio_crypt_ctx()\u0027 line is in a slightly different order.  So this difference is expected, currently.\n\nWe can\u0027t easily upgrade the fscrypt/ext4/f2fs patches on the other ACK branches they depend on blk-crypto; and we can\u0027t upgrade blk-crypto to the upstreamed version without breaking the KMI and because a vendor has objected to it.\n\nI suggest we wait for Satya\u0027s patch series \"[PATCH 0/4] Inline Encryption Support for fscrypt\" to be upstream (in Linus\u0027 tree) in 5.9.  Then we\u0027ll update android-mainline to it, and then I\u0027ll backport it to the other ACK branches as best I can without upgrading blk-crypto.  We *could* do that earlier, but the patches are still subject to change, so it would be better to wait for the final upstreamed versions.",
